Looking into it now, and have a few things to confirm. [~accountid:5aab754b5c335d2a73a795f4] 


As we discussed, the list definitely should not be limited by the categories mentioned above, and we can require the field for all *High* and *Significant* cases and still show it for the rest, just in case. It surely applies to accidents and assaults but also robberies, hijacking, and sexual assaults. There is also a potential of missing something when we have several serious categories appearing under one case.

*So, we’d ask to* {{Specify if any injuries or fatalities have been reported}}*.*

{color:#97a0af}□ First Aid Injury{color}

{color:#97a0af}□ Medical Treatment Injury{color}

{color:#97a0af}□ Injury Impacting Lifestyle{color}

{color:#97a0af}□ Permanent Disability{color}

{color:#97a0af}□ Fatality{color}

{color:#97a0af}□ No Injury{color}

{color:#97a0af}□ Unknown Injury{color}

----

* I would utilise the existing *Reportables* field, meaning we lose visibility for older cases on the Cognito form while maintaining the data in Looker. *If you think we should keep it* - I’ll find a way, that’s just to avoid adding any more weight to the form if it’s not 100% necessary.
* For the same reason, maybe we should not ask about Fatality separately either. It would be good to keep data in a unified format, and also for the agents to have similar questions in different places (accidents).
* It would be a multiple-choice field then, which makes sense to an extent (if we have several parties sustaining different levels of injuries, for example). But seems to be more user-friendly to just choose the highest of injuries. What do you think?
* For Micromobility, we also have the option of “Unknown Injury” as we might not have enough data to determine the extent. Good for keeping it unified as well but might open a door for misuse and inaccuracy.


{color:#97a0af}PS Just for visibility, we will not be capturing the following after implementing the change{color}

* {color:#97a0af}overview of third party damages{color}
* {color:#97a0af}overview of {color}{color:#97a0af}*party*{color}{color:#97a0af} that sustained injuries (Rider/Driver or Third Party){color}

{{Jose,}}
{{I assure you that I'm fully aware of the situation. And therefor I've been working non stop for the last day to find a solution.}}
{{However I'm not to happy with this email and the characterization of the job that we've done. I'll do my best to list this here;}}
{{1. The job is dimensioned after the same specs as the other jobs we've had for other scooter companies. Based on the information about battery capacity provided by you.}}
{{2. Same as above.}}
{{3. The size of the main breaker is not equal to the sum of the breakers it powers, but in accordance with a factor of simultaneity. This was calculated based on an estimation on the different}}
