Hey! Thanks for the input, let me comment one by one:
*(1)* {{PSL_SUPPORT_DATA_DELETION_BY_USER,DATA_DELETION_NO,true,SINGLE_CHOICE,Do you provide a way for users to request that their data is deleted? / No }}{color:#bf2600}- can you please explain why you chose No for data deletion? Users can delete their accounts via CS or on their own. I appreciate we don't fully erase the data from the privacy point of view, but basec account info (name, email, phone) that helps identify a person is deleted.{color}

The full question in the web form is the following:

{quote}Do you provide a way for users to request that some or all of their data is deleted, without requiring them to delete their account? (Optional){quote}

The “without requiring them to delete their account” was the  problematic part from my perspective, but you’re correct – most likely CS has the options to delete _some_ user data, without the user losing their entire account. I’ll update the answer accordingly – then I’ll have to provide a URL from where the users can make the request, I’ll use [this one|https://bolt.eu/en/support/articles/360017309739/].

*(2)* 

{{PSL_DATA_TYPES_AUDIO,PSL_AUDIO,,MULTIPLE_CHOICE,Audio files / Voice or sound recordings}} {color:#bf2600}- for this set of data, we can collect this info when the user contacts CS team via phone. We do log audio of the call.{color}

Ok, I’ll update the response.

*(3)*

{{PSL_ADVERTISING,,MULTIPLE_CHOICE,Data usage and handling (Email address) / Why is this user data shared? Select all that apply. / Advertising or marketing }}{color:#bf2600}- we also use email addresses for marketing comms{color}

Correct, I’ll update this.

*(4)*

{{PSL_ADVERTISING,true,MULTIPLE_CHOICE,Data usage and handling (User IDs) / Why is this user data collected? Select all that apply. / Advertising or marketing -}}{color:#bf2600} can you please describe how we use User ID for adversting and marketing?{color}

User ID is the one field that all Bolt systems are using to communicate with each other. So if Advertising or Marketing has any user targeting at all, most likely User ID is used.

*(5)*

{{PSL_ADVERTISING,,MULTIPLE_CHOICE,Data usage and handling (Phone number) / Why is this user data shared? Select all that apply. / Advertising or marketing }}{color:#bf2600}- we can also use phone numbers for marketing comms (SMS){color}

Hmm, didn’t know this, I’ll update the response.



*(6)*

{{PSL_APP_FUNCTIONALITY,true,MULTIPLE_CHOICE,Data usage and handling (SMS or MMS) / Why is this user data collected? Select all that apply. / App functionality}} {color:#bf2600}- do you mean that we have to send SMS to sign up or log in?{color}

* {color:#bf2600}We also use SMS for advertising and marketing{color}

Yes, app functionality for users signing in. I’ll update the response to also include advertising & marketing

*(7)*

{{PSL_APP_FUNCTIONALITY,true,MULTIPLE_CHOICE,Data usage and handling (App interactions) / Why is this user data collected? Select all that apply. / App functionality }}{color:#bf2600}- can you please explain why app interactions are necessary for app functionality? is there a specific process when the lack of app interaction data will affect the app functions?{color}

This can be interpreted in many ways, but how I looked at it is the following: we’re using “App interactions” to understand user behaviour, which we’ll take into account when building next versions. Maybe this can be covered with having just “Analytics” as the answer.  

*(8)*

{{PSL_APP_FUNCTIONALITY,true,MULTIPLE_CHOICE,Data usage and handling (In-app search history) }}{color:#bf2600}- can you please explain why in-app search history is necessary for app functionality? Usually, choosing this category means that without collecting this data the app will not work properly or work at all. Is this true for this one?{color}

Well, if we don’t collect this data then _one functionality_ of the app doesn’t work properly. Either way, I think we can completely remove “App functionality” and “Personalisation” as answers here, because the “In-app search history” is only stored on the user’s device. This info leaves the device only for “Analytics” purpose.

*(9)*

{{PSL_PERSONALIZATION,,MULTIPLE_CHOICE,Data usage and handling (App interactions) / Why is this user data collected? Select all that apply. / Personalization}} {color:#bf2600}- afaik, we do use app interactions for delivery/market personalization purposes (at least for eaters).{color}

Right, I’ll remove it.

