# what are the are personal data that we will upload to the Bolt platform;

Name, email, phone number.

2. are these data kept separately from other data that Bolt processes;

The personal data provided in the Business Account is treated separately, but will correspond to the personal data of the rider which is processed by Bolt as an independent controller with its own processing purposes.

To clarify, when a Business Customer`s employee or any data subject uses Bolt Business services for a ride, they are treated as a regular user of the Bolt Rider App. The experience of these business riders is almost identical to that of standard riders, with few exceptions such as the provision of an alternative payment option (Bolt Business) and an additional ride category (Business Ride) for these users. Therefore, Bolt independently processes all personal data of these riders as an independent controller with its own processing purposes such as analytics, and in accordance with our [https://bolt.eu/en/privacy/privacy-for-riders/|https://bolt.eu/en/privacy/privacy-for-riders/|smart-link] .

3. where are the servers on which the Bolt platform is located;

Data stored in EU (Germany, Sweden, Ireland).

4. is data transferred outside the EEA;

The data may only be transferred outside of the EEA if: (i) the Business Customer itself is located outside of the EEA, as a consequence of bidirectional data transfer; (ii) or where Bolt engages sub-processors outside of the EEA, always subject to international data transfer safeguards such as the 2021 SCCs.

Please bear in mind that as Bolt will take up the role of a data controller, it will be fully responsible for the engagement of its sub-processors.

Where a Business Customer in the EEA becomes a client of Bolt Operations OÜ, the data transfer between the Business Customer, the international data transfer does not occur.

5. it is absolutely necessary to upload the first and last name or it is possible to upload only the employees' work phone number and e-mail address;

It is also possible to substitute the names with pseudonyms or other identifiers that do not directly indicate the name of an uploaded user.

6. how long does it take for data to be deleted from the platform at the request of RetuRO (persons who no longer have the status of employees);

If Bolt receives a DSR with a request for data deletion, it will comply with it within the timeframe required under the applicable law (i.e. GDPR). 

Normally, the request will be processed and fulfilled within 1 month of its receipt. However, this period can be extended by an additional two months if the request is particularly complex or if Bolt is dealing with a number of requests from the same individual.

Otherwise, Bolt will retain the personal data of the rider in accordance with its data retention practices clarified under the [https://bolt.eu/en/privacy/privacy-for-riders/|https://bolt.eu/en/privacy/privacy-for-riders/|smart-link] 

7. who exactly has access to the uploaded personal data – is it visible to all Bolt partners?;

The information uploaded to the Business Account will only be visible to the Administrator - an individual appointed by the Customer to administer the Business Account.

Bolt may only have access to the Business Account on the condition of a present lawful basis, e.g. where requested by the Business Customer for the purposes of technical support.

Please note that Bolt remains a data controller for the personal data uploaded by the Business Customer, and will process data for its own purposes, e.g., in order to provide services to the Business Customer, to facilitate payments, etc.

Please also note that this will be the personal data provided by the data subject upon sign up with Bolt will be processed by transportation service providers to be able to provide transportation services.

8. are geolocation coordinates transmitted;

Geolocation is collected for all of trips conducted via Bolt, as clarified by our [https://bolt.eu/en/privacy/privacy-for-riders/|https://bolt.eu/en/privacy/privacy-for-riders/|smart-link]  - to enable efficient pick-up and drop-off, and make the journey and route transparent.

By default, only pick up and drop off points are shared with the Business Customer.

9. services are provided only by partners registered in the Bolt platform, and personal data is communicated to them;

Yes - to be able to provide transportation services via Bolt, transportation service providers require verification and establishing contractual (inter alia, data protection) safeguards under the applicable law.

10. how long are the personal data accessible for the Bolt partner, after the provision of the services.

After providing the transportation service, the name and the telephone number (in some countries the number is masked) of the ride-hailing passenger will remain visible to the driver for 24-48 hours.

Rider rating and geolocation data of the passenger will not be visible after the trip. For any details, please refer to Bolt`s [https://bolt.eu/en/privacy/privacy-for-riders/|https://bolt.eu/en/privacy/privacy-for-riders/|smart-link] .

